# tests/semantic_snapshot_lineage_test.tg — third-audit item 11 +
# fourth-audit P0-1/P0-2/P0-3 (the persistent declaration lineage)
# end-to-end lane.
#
# The lineage model lives in tg_compiler/stable_ids.tg (StablePackageId /
# StableModuleId / DeclLineageId / DeclLineageStore / DeclContinuation,
# the move-stable StableDeclId identity over (package, lineage, kind), the
# conservative rebinding and the v2 atomic store), and the snapshot
# builder's store seam lives in tg_compiler/semantic_snapshot.tg
# (snapshot_stamp_decls — the def walk's declaration-stamping stage). This
# test drives snapshot_lineage_lane_check: ONE DeclLineageStore threaded
# across builds of the builder's stamping stage, pinning the fourth-audit
# behaviors —
#   * a moved declaration (a::foo -> b::foo) keeps its StableDeclId;
#   * an explicit DeclContinuation always preserves identity;
#   * the heuristic rename preserves identity only with the
#     immediately-preceding-revision evidence;
#   * a delete observed in one revision followed by an unrelated
#     same-signature creation in a later revision yields different ids;
#   * the v2 save/load restart round-trip preserves the signature digest
#     words (and the v1 legacy body converts with zero sig digests);
#   * reformatting and a signature edit both keep the id;
# plus the unique-match and signature guards. The helper returns mismatch
# rows (empty = the whole lane verifies), the sibling lane-check
# convention.
#
# Run with the repo root as the working directory:
#   tg test tests/semantic_snapshot_lineage_test.tg

use std::test::assert

use tg_compiler::semantic_snapshot::{snapshot_lineage_lane_check}

@test
def test_snapshot_lineage_continuity_lane() -> Unit
  let rows = snapshot_lineage_lane_check()
  assert(rows.len() == 0, "snapshot lineage lane mismatches: " + rows.join("; "))
end
